  sources:
  - name: Kausal Paths Updates (Nov 2026)
    authority: City of Longmont (Francie Kirkjaffe, last saved 2026-11-05)
    url:
    description: "Francie's proposed dataset values for the 2026 update, for both
      scenarios; yellow cells are new. Its Databases sheet also repeats many of the
      model's current values. Sent by Francie Jaffe (City of Longmont); the date is
      when the file was last saved, which approximates when Kausal received it. Years
      covered: 2016-2050.; Attachment: client/OneDrive_1_21-11-2026/Kausal Paths Updates.xlsx;
      Format: .xlsx; Geographic Coverage: City of Longmont, Colorado; Date Last Updated:
      2026-11-05; Updated by: Jouni Tuomisto (register row drafted by Claude, 2026-11-21)"
    edition:
    target: data_point
  - name: Longmont 2024 GHG Inventory, Paths working copy (Sep 2025)
    authority: Kausal (working copy of the city workbook)
    url:
    description: "Kausal's working copy of the July 2025 version of the 2024 inventory
      (jtt = Jouni Tuomisto). Its 'dataset' sheet holds values copied by hand from
      the other sheets, in the Paths dataset format. It is a staging copy, never an
      origin: cite the sheet that each value was copied from. Drive save date 2025-09-28.;
      Attachment: client/Longmont (CO) Client/2025 Paths Update/DATA COLLECTION_Longmont_2024_GHG_Inventory_jtt.xlsx;
      Format: .xlsx; Geographic Coverage: City of Longmont, Colorado; Date Last Updated:
      2025-09-28; Updated by: Jouni Tuomisto (register row drafted by Claude, 2026-11-21)"
    edition:
    target: data_point
  - name: Longmont scenario model, Feb 2023 update
    authority: City of Longmont (scenario workbook created by Nick Russell)
    url:
    description: 'The scenario model behind the first Paths model. It is the origin
      of most action trajectories (fuel switching, vehicle incentives, waste diversion,
      last-mile connections, renewables), the building floor areas and energy-use-intensity
      improvements, the registered EVs, the vehicle miles per vehicle and the electricity
      and gas use by utility. Sent by Francie Jaffe (City of Longmont); the date is
      when the file was last saved, which approximates when Kausal received it. This
      file is byte-identical to client/Longmont_Model_Feb 2023_Update_FINAL(2).xlsx.
      Years covered: 2016-2050.; Attachment: client/Longmont (CO) Client/KP material/Longmont_Model_Feb
      2023_Update_FINAL.xlsx; Format: .xlsx; Geographic Coverage: City of Longmont,
      Colorado; Date Last Updated: 2023-09-12; Updated by: Jouni Tuomisto (register
      row drafted by Claude, 2026-11-21)'
    edition:
    target: data_point
  dataset:
